# macrdp code owners.
#
# Paths listed here auto-request a review from the owner on every PR that
# touches them and — with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled in the
# main-branch protection — cannot be merged without that approval.
#
# The point is the CI/automation directory. Once on `main`, these workflows run
# with repository secrets and a write-scoped token, which makes them the
# highest-value tampering target in the repo; the risk is not an outside
# contributor changing them (nobody but the owner has write access) but a
# workflow edit riding along unnoticed inside a large PR diff. An explicit
# owner approval makes that impossible to miss.
#
# Two protections already exist and are NOT what this file adds:
#   - GITHUB_TOKEN cannot modify .github/workflows/ at all — GitHub withholds
#     the `workflow` scope from it, so no compromised action can rewrite CI.
#   - Fork pull requests run with a read-only token and no access to secrets.

